---
import './intro.css';
const { kind, number } = Astro.props;
const titles = { placement: 'A copy per process, or one shared copy', identity: 'The same product ID can name different cards', burst: 'Four misses before the first fill finishes', memory: 'One large answer takes the place of three cards' };
---
<figure class="ci-figure" data-ci-choice={kind}>
  <figcaption><span>Figure {number}</span> {titles[kind as keyof typeof titles]}</figcaption>
  <div class="ci-scene">
    {kind === 'placement' && <div class="ci-placement">
      <div><p class="ci-panel-label">Local caches · inside the application processes</p><div class="ci-pair"><div class="ci-local"><b>App A</b><div class="ci-box"><b>P7 · GBP 20.00</b><span>Filled by App A</span></div></div><div class="ci-local"><b>App B</b><div class="ci-box"><b>Empty</b><span>App A’s fill is invisible here</span></div></div></div><p>App B’s first request still needs a source read.</p></div>
      <div><p class="ci-panel-label">Shared cache · outside both processes</p><div class="ci-pair"><div class="ci-box"><b>App A</b></div><div class="ci-box"><b>App B</b></div></div><div class="ci-arrow">↘ each lookup crosses the network ↙</div><div class="ci-box ci-shared"><b>Shared P7 · GBP 20.00</b><span>Either app can reuse this fill</span></div></div>
    </div>}
    {kind === 'identity' && <>
      <p><strong>Only the product ID is in the key</strong></p>
      <div class="ci-identity-row"><div class="ci-box"><b>North requests P7</b><code>key: P7</code></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="ci-box"><b>Save GBP 20.00</b><span>North’s card</span></div></div>
      <div class="ci-identity-row"><div class="ci-box"><b>South requests P7</b><code>key: P7</code></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="ci-box ci-wrong"><b>Hit: GBP 20.00</b><span>Wrong shop: south’s price is GBP 18.00</span></div></div>
      <p><strong>Include the context that changes the answer</strong></p>
      <div class="ci-box ci-right"><code>product:v1:north:P7:en-GB:GBP</code><span>North → GBP 20.00</span></div>
      <div class="ci-box ci-right"><code>product:v1:south:P7:en-GB:GBP</code><span>South → GBP 18.00</span></div>
    </>}
    {kind === 'burst' && <>
      <div class="ci-choice"><label for="ci-burst-mode">When P7 is missing</label><select id="ci-burst-mode" data-burst-select><option value="separate">Each caller starts a read</option><option value="shared">Callers share one fill</option></select></div>
      <p>App A receives four requests before any source read finishes.</p>
      <svg class="ci-burst-circuit" viewBox="0 0 600 240" aria-hidden="true">
        {[0,1,2,3].map(i => <g>
          <text class="ci-caller-label" x="0" y={40+i*55}>Caller {i+1}</text>
          <path data-burst-path={i} d={`M 105 ${32+i*55} C 230 ${32+i*55} 260 ${32+i*55} 390 ${32+i*55}`}/>
          <circle data-request-dot={i} cx="0" cy="0" r="7" opacity="0"/>
          <g data-job={i} style={`transform:translateY(${i*55}px)`}><rect x="395" y="14" width="200" height="38" rx="8"/><text x="495" y="40" text-anchor="middle" data-burst-line={i+1}>Source read {i+1}</text></g>
        </g>)}
      </svg>
      <button type="button" class="ci-replay" data-burst-replay>Replay requests</button>
      <p class="ci-budget"><strong data-burst-count>4</strong> source reads · 4 callers waiting</p>
      <p data-burst-explanation aria-live="polite">All four lookups miss. Each caller starts the same work before a saved copy exists.</p>
    </>}
    {kind === 'memory' && <>
      <div class="ci-choice"><label for="ci-memory-mode">Store the large answer?</label><select id="ci-memory-mode" data-memory-select><option value="yes">Yes · remove three cards</option><option value="no">No · return it without caching</option></select></div>
      <p class="ci-budget">4 KiB cache budget · four 1 KiB cards fit</p>
      <p>Before the large answer arrives</p><div class="ci-memory-bar"><span>P7<small>1 KiB</small></span><span>P3<small>1 KiB</small></span><span>P9<small>1 KiB</small></span><span>P40<small>1 KiB</small></span></div>
      <p>After the decision</p><div class="ci-memory-bar" data-memory-bar><span>P7<small>1 KiB</small></span><span class="ci-large">Large result<small>3 KiB</small></span></div>
      <p>The next requests ask for P3, P9 and P40.</p><ul class="ci-outcomes"><li data-memory-result>P3: miss · P9: miss · P40: miss</li><li><strong data-memory-reads>3</strong> source reads return</li></ul>
      <p data-memory-explanation aria-live="polite">Keeping the large result removes P3, P9 and P40. No request reuses the large result in this trace.</p>
    </>}
  </div>
  <p class="ci-caption">{kind === 'placement' ? 'The same card, placed in two ways. Source calls are described below the local caches; the shared drawing isolates the extra lookup hop.' : kind === 'identity' ? 'Both shops have a product named P7, but they own different prices. No source update is needed to produce this wrong hit.' : kind === 'burst' ? 'An invented overlap within App A. Sharing one fill combines this key’s work; it does not remove the waiting callers or coalesce work in another process.' : 'An invented byte budget and request trace. Sizes include keys and bookkeeping. The chosen removals illustrate the cost of admission; this is not a prediction of Redis’s eviction order.'}</p>
  {(kind === 'burst' || kind === 'memory') && <details><summary>Comparison as text</summary><p>{kind === 'burst' ? 'Without shared work, four callers make four source reads. With one fill shared inside App A, caller 1 starts the source read and callers 2–4 wait for its result. All four receive that result when it completes.' : 'Four 1 KiB cards fill a 4 KiB cache. Storing a 3 KiB result removes three cards. The next requests need those cards, so all three miss. Declining to cache the large result keeps all four cards; the same next requests hit. The large result was returned to its original caller in both cases.'}</p></details>}
</figure>
<script>
  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ci-choice="burst"]')) {
    const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-burst-select]')!;
    const flights: Animation[] = [];
    const show = () => {
      const shared = select.value === 'shared';
      flights.splice(0).forEach(flight=>flight.cancel());
      root.querySelectorAll<SVGPathElement>('[data-burst-path]').forEach((path,i) => {
        const start = 32+i*55, end = shared ? 114 : start;
        path.setAttribute('d',`M 105 ${start} C 230 ${start} 260 ${end} 390 ${end}`);
        const dot = root.querySelector<SVGCircleElement>(`[data-request-dot="${i}"]`)!;
        if (!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) flights.push(dot.animate([
          {transform:`translate(105px,${start}px)`,opacity:0},
          {transform:`translate(170px,${start}px)`,opacity:1,offset:.25},
          {transform:`translate(325px,${end}px)`,opacity:1,offset:.8},
          {transform:`translate(390px,${end}px)`,opacity:0}
        ],{duration:1100,delay:i*100,easing:'ease-in-out'}));
        const job = root.querySelector<SVGGElement>(`[data-job="${i}"]`)!;
        job.style.transform = `translateY(${shared ? 82 : i*55}px)`;
        job.style.opacity = shared && i>0 ? '0' : '1';
      });
      root.querySelectorAll('[data-burst-line]').forEach((el,i) => { el.textContent = shared ? 'One shared read' : `Source read ${i+1}`; });
      root.querySelector('[data-burst-count]')!.textContent = shared ? '1' : '4';
      root.querySelector('[data-burst-explanation]')!.textContent = shared ? 'Caller 1 starts the fill. Callers 2–4 share its result when it finishes. A failed read also has to end their wait.' : 'All four lookups miss. Each caller starts the same work before a saved copy exists.';
    };
    select.addEventListener('change',show);
    root.querySelector('[data-burst-replay]')!.addEventListener('click',show);
  }
  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ci-choice="memory"]')) {
    root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-memory-select]')?.addEventListener('change', event => {
      const admit = (event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value === 'yes';
      const bar = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-bar]')!;
      const old = new Map([...bar.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(':scope > span:not([data-leaving])')].map(cell => [cell.firstChild!.textContent!, {cell:cell.cloneNode(true) as HTMLElement, rect:cell.getBoundingClientRect()}]));
      const origin = bar.getBoundingClientRect();
      bar.replaceChildren();
      for (const name of admit ? ['P7','Large result'] : ['P7','P3','P9','P40']) {
        const cell = document.createElement('span');
        const size = document.createElement('small');
        cell.textContent = name;
        size.textContent = name === 'Large result' ? '3 KiB' : '1 KiB';
        if (name === 'Large result') cell.className = 'ci-large';
        cell.append(size); bar.append(cell);
      }
      if (!matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        for (const cell of bar.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(':scope > span')) {
          const name = cell.firstChild!.textContent!;
          if (!old.has(name)) cell.animate([{opacity:0,transform:'translateY(-32px) scale(.85)'},{opacity:1,transform:'translateY(0) scale(1)'}],{duration:650,easing:'cubic-bezier(.2,.8,.3,1)'});
          old.delete(name);
        }
        for (const {cell,rect} of old.values()) {
          cell.dataset.leaving = '';
          Object.assign(cell.style,{position:'absolute',left:`${rect.left-origin.left}px`,top:`${rect.top-origin.top}px`,width:`${rect.width}px`,height:`${rect.height}px`,boxSizing:'border-box',margin:'0',zIndex:'2'});
          cell.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true'); bar.append(cell);
          cell.animate([{opacity:1,transform:'translateY(0)'},{opacity:0,transform:'translateY(34px) rotate(5deg)'}],{duration:450,easing:'ease-in',fill:'forwards'}).finished.finally(()=>cell.remove());
        }
      }
      root.querySelector('[data-memory-result]')!.textContent = admit ? 'P3: miss · P9: miss · P40: miss' : 'P3: hit · P9: hit · P40: hit';
      root.querySelector('[data-memory-reads]')!.textContent = admit ? '3' : '0';
      root.querySelector('[data-memory-explanation]')!.textContent = admit ? 'Keeping the large result removes P3, P9 and P40. No request reuses the large result in this trace.' : 'Return the large result to its caller, but keep the four cards. All three later requests reuse their saved answers.';
    });
  }
</script>
